# Theorem T2 (R-SI-1, "no star"): the shipped ternary MAC synthesizes to a
# netlist containing ZERO multiplier cells and ZERO DSP48 primitives, while
# the golden reference -- which computes the same function (see T1) -- needs a
# multiplier.  This is the structural half of the ternary claim: T1 says the
# function is exact integer MAC, T2 says we get it without a multiplier.
#
# Run: yosys -s prove_no_multiplier.ys

read_verilog ../verilog/ternary_mac_synth.v
synth_xilinx -abc9 -nocarry -arch xc7 -top ternary_mac_top
tee -o dut_stat.txt stat
design -reset

read_verilog ternary_mac_golden.v
synth_xilinx -abc9 -nocarry -arch xc7 -top ternary_mac_golden
tee -o golden_stat.txt stat
